  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 155 PM EST Mon Nov 16 2026\nShortwave energy is moving along the northern Gulf coast region this \nafternoon while surface high pressure remains to our north and a \nweak low pressure area tries to form over the eastern Gulf. This \nsetup has kept breezy northeast winds in place across the local \narea, with a few showers continuing to move onshore. Expect this \ntrend to continue through the rest of today and tonight. Rain \nchances increase even more starting Tuesday and continue through \nmuch of the week as these features slowly make their way eastward \nand eventually off the northeast Florida coast this weekend.\n\nAs far as rainfall, the Weather Prediction Center continues to \nhighlight east central Florida in a marginal/slight (level 1/2 of 4) \nrisk for excessive rainfall for tomorrow through Friday as the setup \nwill likely allow some heavier rain bands to develop over the \ncoastal waters and extend over the coast. Though confidence in \nreceiving flooding rainfall has increased, there is still a decent \namount of uncertainty with the overall forecast as we'll have to see \nwhere and how strong the low will be as it moves over the region.",
